      "description": "Only when you have no Assistable API key: start signing in. Returns verification_uri_complete and user_code; send the person that link (or the code) so they can sign in to Assistable, pick the account and approve. Then call assistable_connect_finish with device_code every interval seconds until it returns api_key. If they have no account, the link lets them sign up first.",
      "execution": {
        "taskSupport": "forbidden"
      },
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "properties": {
          "client_name": {
            "description": "Your agent's name, shown to the person approving, e.g. Hermes.",
            "maxLength": 60,
            "minLength": 1,
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "assistable_connect"
    },
    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "readOnlyHint": false
      },
      "description": "Check an assistable_connect sign-in. error.code authorization_pending means the person has not approved yet: wait interval seconds and call again. On approval it returns api_key once: use it as the Authorization: Bearer header for this MCP server (mcp_url) and keep it safe; it cannot be shown again.",
      "execution": {
        "taskSupport": "forbidden"
      },
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
        "properties": {
